The indexed separated sum of a neighbourhood system, assuming every neighbourhood is nonempty, is the system on sum tokens whose neighbourhoods are the master token set, the unit copy, or a letter-copy of a neighbourhood. The master is that token set and contains the empty token. Each kind of neighbourhood is contained in the master. The intersection of two neighbourhoods again contains a neighbourhood: a master absorbs the other factor, two unit copies remain the unit copy, a unit copy is disjoint from a letter-copy, two letter-copies at one letter meet in a letter-copy of an intersection after the master, the unit copy, and a foreign letter have been excluded, and two letter-copies at distinct letters are disjoint.
